    <tags>image-optimizer image-compression image-converter webp avif jpeg-xl mozjpeg oxipng ssimulacra2 mcp foss cross-platform</tags>
    <summary>Lighter images, just as good: a free, open-source image optimizer for WebP, AVIF, JPEG XL, JPEG and PNG.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Apolo is a free, open-source image optimizer. It compresses and converts images to WebP, AVIF, JPEG XL, JPEG and PNG on your own computer: nothing is uploaded anywhere.

Instead of guessing a quality number, you see what you lose before you save: a slider, side by side or a difference map, with the SSIMULACRA 2 score of every result. You can also ask for a target such as "no visible loss", and Apolo finds the lowest quality that reaches it, photo by photo.

## Features

- The official engines (libwebp, MozJPEG, OxiPNG, libavif and libjxl): the same file, byte for byte, as cwebp, cjpeg, oxipng, avifenc and cjxl.
- Whole folders in parallel, to one or more formats at once. It always writes new files and never overwrites your originals.
- Resize, crop and reduce the palette. Opens iPhone HEIC photos.
- A command line, `apolo`, and an MCP server, `apolo-mcp`, so Claude, Cursor and other AI agents can optimize images for you.
- In English and Spanish, with light and dark mode.

## Package notes

- Installs the official NSIS installer from the GitHub Release, silently, for x64 or ARM64 depending on the machine.
- The installer is per-user: it goes into the profile of the account that runs `choco install`.
- Apolo checks GitHub for new versions and offers to update itself; the package can lag behind until the next version is approved here.
- Requires Windows 10 or 11 and the Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime (the installer downloads it if it's missing).
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://apolo.webcafeina.com/en/whats-new/</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
